<title>SINGAPORE: Sri Lanka sells fuel oil to BP at minus $14.75/T.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka sells fuel oil to BP at minus $14.75/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's state-owned Ceylon Petroleum Corp (CPC) sold by tender 20,000 tonnes of fuel oil to British Petroleum at a discount of $14.75 per tonne to Singapore spot quotes, a CPC source said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The 180-centistoke grade, 3.5 percent sulphur fuel oil will be for July 22-23 lifting on a free-on-board (fob) Colombo basis, the source said.</p>
<p>The tender closed on July 15.</p>
<p>In its last tender, CPC sold the same amount of 177-cst, 3.5-percent sulphur fuel oil at a discount of $12.50 per tonne to Singapore spot quotes for late May lifting, fob Colombo.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870 3571)</p>
